            <ArticleTitle>Psychogenic chest pain in children.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>788-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Thirty-six children with psychogenic chest pain were studied. A specific stressful situation causally related to the onset of symptoms could be identified in most patients with psychogenic chest pain. Fifty-five per cent of children with psychogenic chest pain had a history of other recurrent somatic complaints and 30% had a history of significant sleep disturbances.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
